{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"category","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Category"}]},"title_text":"Category","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"category.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","category"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"category"}]},{"Text":" "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C)"}},{"Text":" consists of"}]},{"Enum":{"numbering":null,"start":1,"tight":true,"items":[{"number":null,"body":{"Inline":[{"Text":"A type of objects "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C)_0"}}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Inline":[{"Text":"For each pair of objects "},{"Math":{"src":"x, y : cal(C)_0"}},{"Text":" a "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"set"}]},{"Text":" of morphisms "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C) (x, y)"}},{"Text":". We may simply write a morphism with an arrow, denote "},{"Math":{"src":"f : cal(C) (x, y)"}},{"Text":" as "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":" or "},{"Math":{"src":"x limits(->)^f y"}},{"Text":" or similar"}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Inline":[{"Text":"A composition operation on morphisms. For "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"g : y -> z"}},{"Text":", there is a morphism "},{"Math":{"src":"f ⋆ g : x -> z"}}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Inline":[{"Text":"For each "},{"Math":{"src":"x : cal(C)_0"}},{"Text":", an identity morphism "},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"id\")_x : x -> x"}}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Left-unitality of composition: for all "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":", an equality"}]},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"idL\")_f : sans(\"id\")_x ⋆ f = f"}}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Right-unitality of composition: for all "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":", an equality"}]},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"idR\")_f : f ⋆ sans(\"id\")_y = f"}}]}},{"number":null,"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Associativity of composition: for all "},{"Math":{"src":"f : x -> y"}},{"Text":", "},{"Math":{"src":"g : y -> z"}},{"Text":", "},{"Math":{"src":"h : z -> w"}},{"Text":", an equality"}]},{"Math":{"src":"sans(\"assoc\")_(f, g, h) : (f ⋆ g) ⋆ h = f ⋆ (g ⋆ h)"}}]}}]}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Concretely, the definition above is meant to model "},{"Link":{"url":"https://github.com/agda/cubical/blob/master/Cubical/Categories/Category/Base.agda","body":[{"Text":"the one used in the Cubical standard library"}]}},{"Text":" "},{"Cite":{"key":"cubicalagdalib","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"However, the notion of category is flexible. Depending on the context, we may be talking of small, locally small, wild, or any other kind of category that may augment which things we require to be (homotopy) sets, which things we require to be small types, etc. For the most part, the same idea of a category will apply across all of these settings."}]}]}}}]}}
